      "problem": "Which of the following number lines represents the inequality $x\\ge -2?$",
      "worked_solution": "The condition $x\\ge -2$ implies that $x$ can be any value that is **greater than or equal to** $-2.$\n\n To represent this on a number line:\n\n- We draw a **closed** circle at $x=-2.$\n\n- Then, we draw an arrow starting from $-2$ and going to the **right**.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149933/assets/4be757012411ef309bb4c224d874ce97741efe174395566eca760d0b37766df3.png)",
